age`:"",`locator`:"data/Ring-adhesion.csv",`quote`:"Ring-adhesion.csv",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"呈现状态\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:e8b49fbfdae596c8",`source`:"shipkg:observation:59f88fb7c81e",`target`:"shipkg:fault:911e598cd781",`properties`:{`name`:"呈现状态",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:e8b49fbfdae596c8",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"dataset_label",`certainty_zh`:"数据集标签",`evidence_id`:"ev:d61287b84a7d06e2",`source_file`:"Azimuth_Thruster_CBM_Dataset.zip",`source_url`:"https://zenodo.org/records/20101612",`page`:"",`locator`:"table3_lti_by_fault_type_anonymised.csv:row11",`quote`:"System / engine-family case=CAT C7 engine case A BB / CAT C7 shaftline case A; Fault or condition=Additive depletion; Detection/event reference=Oil-led alert at Month -1.0; ND (oil-led); Reference class=ND (oil-led); Recommended CBM action=Oil-led CBM; 500 h vibration / 125 h oil; Included in mechanical LTI summary=no",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"呈现状态\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:ea408031a5706e10",`source`:"shipkg:dataset:19e52eb49467",`target`:"shipkg:fault:ebfac27b4d41",`properties`:{`name`:"呈现状态",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:ea408031a5706e10",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"simulated",`certainty_zh`:"仿真状态",`evidence_id`:"ev:a50b62c3875a33d5",`source_file`:"TSRF_main.zip",`source_url`:"https://github.com/TS-RF/TSRF",`page`:"",`locator`:"data/Ring-wear.csv",`quote`:"Ring-wear.csv",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"呈现状态\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:SHOWS_CONDITION {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_42 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:1a8d22464c3d1c3c",`source`:"shipkg:condition:7fb8a1a33328",`target`:"shipkg:fault:cdf116929c39",`properties`:{`name`:"触发",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:1a8d22464c3d1c3c",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:91f76498fecf4e21",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"43",`locator`:"PDF page 43",`quote`:"cating oil. In principle this was an entirely sensible precaution to protect the high voltage pod motor from damage. However, the low position of the bilge sensor meant that it could be activated by a relatively small amount of liquid that accumulated within the pod. Since the bilge suction probably did not extend low enough for the automatic bilge pumps to effectively pump the water out, it is likely the vessel’s motion in heavy weather caused the small amoun",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"触发\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": true}"}},{`id`:"edge:a224f41b8b7d6b98",`source`:"shipkg:fault:999defd690d8",`target`:"shipkg:symptom:674bee46af7f",`properties`:{`name`:"触发",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:a224f41b8b7d6b98",`case_id`:"sd2013_12_oily_rag",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:0e28dc346f51844d",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"41",`locator`:"PDF page 41",`quote`:"ifold and catch fire. The small fire then ignited the engine high temperature alarm cabling loom, causing it to short circuit and set off the alarm in the wheelhouse (Figure 2). The functional fire and smoke alarm sensors were some distance from the fire, and the smoke and heat had not migrated that far by the time the master noticed the smoke on the camera monitor.",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"触发\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": true}"}},{`id`:"edge:a5a324438d9fb4aa",`source`:"shipkg:fault:e97eee073fc6",`target`:"shipkg:fault:c830e7992f26",`properties`:{`name`:"触发",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:a5a324438d9fb4aa",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:5d3cde311b090a6a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"42",`locator`:"PDF page 42",`quote`:"e rpm of each pod’s propulsion motor very rapidly increased and exceeded the preset overspeed limitation. The pod’s PCS therefore automatically tripped the power to its motor to prevent it being damaged. Spirit of Discovery’s engineers could likely have quickly reset the port and starboard motors and restored the vessel’s propulsion had the propulsion motor overspeed trips been the only issue. However",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"触发\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": true}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:TRIGGERS {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_43 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:1baaf26081652c9a",`source`:"shipkg:condition:a40db02fd2fa",`target`:"shipkg:action:6e0e5173ee8f",`properties`:{`name`:"削弱效果",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:1baaf26081652c9a",`case_id`:"sd2016_09_cpp_response",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:1ed28429bcfc3816",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"tion of this button bypassed the feedback control system, giving direct control of pitch to the pitch control lever. However, the master was not familiar with its use, and therefore lost the opportunity to bring the vessel back under control before it struck the quay. It was also revealed during the investigation that the system parameters for astern pitch control had been incorrectly set duri",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"削弱效果\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:23d24efd05e23e3e",`source`:"shipkg:condition:7a0e4d2405ef",`target`:"shipkg:action:9fa28e4c4571",`properties`:{`name`:"削弱效果",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:23d24efd05e23e3e",`case_id`:"windcat8_port_engine_2017",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:e678a8a1bb3f1aec",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_01_Windcat8_bearing_failure_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/683922/MAIBInvReport01_2018.pdf",`page`:"11",`locator`:"PDF page 11",`quote`:"ire resulted from the ignition of oil vapour released from the damaged crankcase and did not spread beyond the port engine. • The fixed fire-fighting system was rendered ineffective because not all the port engine space vents were closed prior to its release. • The safety of the embarked technicians was given a high priority. ACTION TAKEN Windcat Workboats BV Ltd has: • Instructed crews on board vessels fitted with Volvo Penta D16 engines to stop the affected eng",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"削弱效果\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:REDUCES_EFFECTIVENESS_OF {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_44 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:1c38937cd6ac3b2a",`source`:"shipkg:condition:96f46a0b1ef9",`target`:"shipkg:condition:4277de3a84c9",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:1c38937cd6ac3b2a",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:412268fc761e9960",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"27",`locator`:"PDF page 27",`quote`:"ions. 2.4 HOT SPOT MONITORING Stena’s practice of measuring the temperature of running engines using an infrared spot thermometer had not identified the significant hazard posed by exposed surfaces of over 220°C that still existed post-accident after the insulation and shielding were replaced. The use of infrared spot thermometers in engine spaces limited their effectiveness as they could only prov",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:21c269f536ddda50",`source`:"shipkg:condition:db2e89c50479",`target`:"shipkg:fault:b2aa91be158b",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:21c269f536ddda50",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:3bea0430b472030b",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"64",`locator`:"PDF page 64",`quote`:"current imbalance transformer were tested during manufacture, subsequent tests of the system were by secondary current injection, bypassing the windings. As the IAS did not specifically register which rank of the HF had developed an imbalance current, it was not possible to confirm if the current imbalance transformers on rank 1 1.3 had ever worked in service. It is concerning th",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:45c48f589ff003ad",`source`:"shipkg:condition:290bfe38530e",`target`:"shipkg:fault:c44e6c4545bf",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:45c48f589ff003ad",`case_id`:"sd2016_05_cpp_backup",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:2d8d8f05ec0d8390",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"tective covers over safety- critical buttons, switches and knobs. 2. The master was confident that he had control of his CPPs and did not look at the pitch indicators located on the control consoles. Had he done so he would have realised the starboard CPP was not responding to his orders. 3. The ship’s engineers recognised that something was untoward well before the master had committed to his",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:46fbc1fad6f5bc77",`source`:"shipkg:condition:19ae439543bd",`target`:"shipkg:fault:5f59e6b3ca42",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:46fbc1fad6f5bc77",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me_2017",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:9094aa614ec060db",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"ntrolled environment and transferring it complete into the engine room would have reduced the likelihood of debris ingress. • The engine was not fitted with a wear detector, so there was no means of receiving a warning before the engine failed. • The essential services switchboard aft circuit breaker had been left in manual mode, resulting in the loss of power to critical equipment, including the fixed fire-fighting system. ACTION TAKEN Wightli",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:6ec0a6e6cf79dfff",`source`:"shipkg:condition:bdbca1b8295e",`target`:"shipkg:fault:439f73a406a0",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:6ec0a6e6cf79dfff",`case_id`:"sd2013_03_turning_gear",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:6522054ba5597880",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"Although the indicator for the turning gear, which was sited on the control panel, showed that the turning gear was in, this was poorly illuminated and was not seen by the engineer. When the main engine start button was pressed to turn the engine on compressed air, a loud bang was heard; the turning gear interlock, the last remaining safety barrier, had failed to work. The resulting damage t",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:7fcc0c54724f2e91",`source`:"shipkg:condition:4a944c6dd633",`target`:"shipkg:condition:2d0261049d78",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:7fcc0c54724f2e91",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:d82fabc2bbd1fcf1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"e the aft HF from the electrical network. It was not possible to determine the exact cause of the subsequent blackout because the option for storing historical data concerning blackouts was not chosen at build. However, it is considered most likely that the disruption within the aft HF at the time of the accident caused general instability in the electrical network which could not be contained and led to the generators shuttin",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:978fd5dea39c2ab2",`source`:"shipkg:condition:4ae93bca9f29",`target`:"shipkg:fault:3349e319bedc",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:978fd5dea39c2ab2",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:9d1bc8efb3c65396",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"27",`locator`:"PDF page 27",`quote`:"’s main engine fuel systems were historically reported in the vessel’s DOCMAP system. However, this had stopped over time and the crew instead repaired the leaks and recorded them locally in the engine room logbook. The relatively high turnover and heavy workload of engine room crew had resulted in defect reporting being considered a low priority, which had led to the requirements in SMS document SMM-0255 not bein",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:ab901de38913b7d7",`source`:"shipkg:condition:133adfa97595",`target`:"shipkg:consequence:81fff36694d8",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:ab901de38913b7d7",`case_id`:"sd2016_22_cooling_pipe",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:6a6ede2b06a7fa26",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"60",`locator`:"PDF page 60",`quote`:"are supper. Although the bilge alarm operated as designed, with no one present in the wheelhouse to either see or hear it, it was not detected in time to save the vessel. Never leave the wheelhouse unmanned when underway; doing so is in contravention of the COLREGs and puts you and your vessel at risk. 2. The crew were instructed to enter the accommodation to collect lifejackets in preparation fo",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:bd71a40255f6239a",`source`:"shipkg:condition:94ebbaf1c3c4",`target`:"shipkg:consequence:775549e4c085",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:bd71a40255f6239a",`case_id`:"sd2013_12_oily_rag",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:db9d3c4ba46b3f43",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"41",`locator`:"PDF page 41",`quote`:"off the alarm in the wheelhouse (Figure 2). The functional fire and smoke alarm sensors were some distance from the fire, and the smoke and heat had not migrated that far by the time the master noticed the smoke on the camera monitor.",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:e4dc29615b38ae3d",`source`:"shipkg:condition:4fe499c68172",`target`:"shipkg:fault:1e5a23a200ad",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:e4dc29615b38ae3d",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:a761595279b52f7c",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"ey need to be checked to ensure they continue to function correctly. However, in the case of Pride of Canterbury these valves had never been tested or inspected since the ship was constructed 23 years previously. The LIPS CPP system manual provided some maintenance instructions, including annual testing of pressure safety valve (PSV1) and the back pressure valve (PSV3). However, how this",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:e6a307f3b94eadaf",`source`:"shipkg:condition:7d61f4e32250",`target`:"shipkg:fault:8027eb707475",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:e6a307f3b94eadaf",`case_id`:"sd2013_03_turning_gear",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:4ed3569c8bb32f4f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"18",`locator`:"PDF page 18",`quote`:"CASE 3 17MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 The Lessons 1. The turning gear interlock had not been included within the planned maintenance system on board and there was no record of it having been tested. 2. Control console illumination panels are vital to the safe operation of machinery and should therefore be tested regularly. If problems with visual indication or warnin",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:eb00e74b105c9e6b",`source`:"shipkg:condition:4dcab8c954bb",`target`:"shipkg:fault:1e5a23a200ad",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:eb00e74b105c9e6b",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:7058770c39736963",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"30",`locator`:"PDF page 30",`quote`:"24 the valves and their refitting was deemed an unnecessary measure. However, the oil sampling programme had not identified the wear in the back pressure valve as it had, most likely, occurred gradually over a long period of time. 2.3.3 Pipework joints and shielding Whereas the main components of Pride of Canterbury’s CPP system were supplied after testing by",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:f08fa036f145759a",`source`:"shipkg:fault:b2aa91be158b",`target`:"shipkg:fault:5737f3610967",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:f08fa036f145759a",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:ab39293c5f3260fc",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"64",`locator`:"PDF page 64",`quote`:"ious problems. 2.4.5 Current imbalance detection system The capacitor exploded because the inoperative imbalance detection system could not identify the deterioration of the capacitors. The failure of the imbalance system’s current transformer remained undetected for what could have been several years. It is certain that this system was not working in 2008 when Converteam detected two defective capacitors durin",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:LIMITS_DETECTION_OF {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_45 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:1c6b7f69dbb6868b",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:2ed46421a269",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:4b3a114ff733",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:1c6b7f69dbb6868b",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:8c30394060f9cd2e",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"30",`locator`:"PDF page 30",`quote`:"d, most likely, occurred gradually over a long period of time. 2.3.3 Pipework joints and shielding Whereas the main components of Pride of Canterbury’s CPP system were supplied after testing by the manufacturer, the interconnecting pipework was supplied and fitted by the shipyard when the vessel was constructed. Although the manufacturer’s drawings specified a particular type",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:1d2adeeba2026d76",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:9f37ba0a1a27",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:4b3a114ff733",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:1d2adeeba2026d76",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:57049bc52d7488e2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"7",`locator`:"PDF page 7",`quote`:"mage to the port main engine room and rendered one of its four main engines inoperative for several weeks. The fire was caused by fuel leaking under pressure from the fuel system of main engine number 3 and igniting on an exposed hot surface. No one was injured and there was no pollution. The investigation found that the fuel had ignited on part of the engine’s exhaust system that had",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:22cc33617b12a5be",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:ce08d017f5c9",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:3309438ef854",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:22cc33617b12a5be",`case_id`:"windcat8_port_engine_2017",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:4e45851ecc9eb9f4",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_01_Windcat8_bearing_failure_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/683922/MAIBInvReport01_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"and no injuries. The MAIB investigation identified that the catastrophic damage to Windcat 8’s port main engine was caused by the failure of a piston connecting rod big end shell bearing, which resulted in the connecting rod assembly releasing and penetrating through the engine crankcase. The investigation also identified that: • A high oil temperature alarm prior to the engine failure warranted a more cautious a",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:2c6f1a13391788b4",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:2ee30864aa2d",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:1baadd7689d1",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:2c6f1a13391788b4",`case_id`:"kommandor_susan_dg1_2025",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:01f3913bd9c46899",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"f Forth, Scotland on 25 January 2025 SUMMARY At 1305 on 25 January 2025, the site investigation vessel Kommandor Susan suffered a catastrophic failure of a diesel generator engine while conducting sea trials in the Firth of Forth, Scotland. The failure resulted in an engine room fire and a complete power blackout. The crew responded promptly, extinguished the fire and mustered safely. The vessel lost propu",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:3a331549a6929c8a",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:a81974e78c4c",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:f28be4be5375",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:3a331549a6929c8a",`case_id`:"sd2016_14_sea_valve",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:b7715f5c139d9453",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"33 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 14 Fail to Plan, Plan to Fail Narrative On a fine day, a general cargo vessel was on passage with a cargo of limestone. The master was on watch on the bridge. In the engine room, the chief engineer, motorman and a seaman were undertaking maintenance on one of the two main ballast pumps; the chief engineer",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:3f851a4be0d6c03d",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:3fb5a9c954ef",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:4b3a114ff733",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:3f851a4be0d6c03d",`case_id`:"sd2016_08_generator_oil",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:7e21ab64015c1360",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"26",`locator`:"PDF page 26",`quote`:"19 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 8 Maintenance Induced Fire Narrative A fully loaded ro-ro passenger ferry was en route to its next port when the engineers in the control room acknowledged a low oil pressure alarm on one of the generators (Figure 1). On the CCTV they observed that oil from this generator was spraying on to the adjacen",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:558dfa355f3dab82",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:fa10fa0f80d3",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:4b3a114ff733",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:558dfa355f3dab82",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me2_2018",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:4846a9af2b7e6456",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"S 3.1 SAFETY ISSUES DIRECTLY CONTRIBUTING TO THE ACCIDENTS THAT HAVE BEEN ADDRESSED OR RESULTED IN RECOMMENDATIONS 1. Wight Sky’s ME2 failed catastrophically due to a sudden loss of lubricating oil supply to its number five main journal bearing and number four crankpin. [2.3.1] 2. The oilway to the main journal and crankpin was blocked off when the bearing shells turned in their housing. Poor fuel combustion, the presence of silic",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:583c466331d08fec",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:fa10fa0f80d3",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:4b3a114ff733",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:583c466331d08fec",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me4_2018",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:3ca79df2a0332a1a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"igh levels of vibration, and contaminated lubricating oil might all have contributed to the event failure. [2.3.1] 3. Wight Sky’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Volvo Penta’s factory in Sweden. Two of the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:744ea296ee760db7",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:fa10fa0f80d3",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:4b3a114ff733",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:744ea296ee760db7",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me_2017",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:19d0b2283f62b511",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"examination conducted by the vessel’s engine maker, Volvo Penta UK, concluded that the most probable trigger for the failure was debris in the engine’s oil channels following rebuild. The MAIB investigation established the following: • The engine had been completely rebuilt and failed after 5½ hours of operation. • The vessel’s soft patches 1 had not been removed, necessitating the engine to be lowered piecem",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:7cfabc6ce5030514",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:808ea34d5772",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:4b3a114ff733",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:7cfabc6ce5030514",`case_id`:"sd2016_05_cpp_backup",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:96829240b9d90823",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"19",`locator`:"PDF page 19",`quote`:"12 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 5 Propelled Onto the Berth Narrative A large roll-on roll-off passenger ferry, operating on its regular route between two European ports, suffered significant damage when it made heavy contact with a linkspan as it was being manoeuvred onto its berth. There were over 500 passengers and crew on board but no",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:807b66dfcdd4bff8",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:205954d6d86e",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:f28be4be5375",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:807b66dfcdd4bff8",`case_id`:"sd2013_05_missing_filter",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:7116308e5054c090",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"CASE 5 20 MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative A fully loaded cargo ship departed port and proceeded on her voyage. Several days into the passage, the oil mist detector (OMD) on the medium speed diesel main engine alarmed. The duty engineer investigated but could not find any fault with the engine. He",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:949e25f70b41b18e",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:5466bfcfc864",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:bbb73c8d697d",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:949e25f70b41b18e",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:c3429f0fc22579e1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"42",`locator`:"PDF page 42",`quote`:"e vessel’s heading. Given the weather conditions at the time, it is almost certain that Spirit of Discovery’s pitching caused the propellers to come out of the water. This caused a sudden reduction in torque on the propulsion motor and led to a very rapid increase in the motors’ rpm. The engine alarm and monitoring system recorded that, immediately before their shutdown, the rpm of each pod’s",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:97c0058fae4597a7",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:ea737bd37b3c",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:ba47bdb9e2f3",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:97c0058fae4597a7",`case_id`:"sd2016_22_cooling_pipe",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:fe1c60aff6da4452",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"59",`locator`:"PDF page 59",`quote`:"52 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 22 Supper Would Have Been on Time if the Vessel Had Not Sunk Narrative A 24m steel hulled fishing trawler, with a crew of six, was fishing in calm seas when its engine began to make unusual noises. No-one was in the wheelhouse; the skipper, who was on watch, had gone to the mess room to prepare supper and the majority of the crew wer",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:a1685388bf6cc014",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:5d3e7e7eb367",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:21e082f35a40",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:a1685388bf6cc014",`case_id`:"sd2013_03_turning_gear",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:b840391c6c40b9b8",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"CASE 3 15MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative A specialist cargo ship was in port loading a dangerous cargo. As a precaution, the vessel’s slow speed diesel main engine had been tested and was kept at a heightened state of readiness. This involved the fuel being shut off, the main engine indicator",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:a37f177aceb87df3",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:e9dd95119f56",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:3c0f99655948",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:a37f177aceb87df3",`case_id`:"sd2016_09_cpp_response",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:e1dce2948e24adc9",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"22 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 9 Sluggish Pitch Control Causes Serious Accident Narrative A chemical tanker was being manoeuvred to its designated jetty. As the vessel approached the quay, the pilot ordered an astern movement to enable a turn into the lock. The vessel did not respond and continued to proceed ahead. Despite placing the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:ab0e830c01ac6e7b",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:db8f8f17b349",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:2973e45389fb",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:ab0e830c01ac6e7b",`case_id`:"finlandia_seaways_me_2018",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:eb8d9ba0db21fede",`source_file`:"MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured",`page`:"9",`locator`:"PDF page 9",`quote`:"ent and Incident Investigation Division and the engine manufacturer, MAN Diesel and Turbo SE. The investigation identified that a fracture of the connecting rod small end had led to the sudden failure of the main engine. The investigation also found that the method used to replace the connecting rod small end piston pin bearing bushes by the vessel manager’s maintenance support contractor had intr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:cfa8f58ac479e8ae",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:3cb736742ac6",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:bbb73c8d697d",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:cfa8f58ac479e8ae",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:af6ff177f229c6a2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"e suppression spray heads were activated, one in the aft harmonic filter room and the other in the aft main switchboard room. The explosion was triggered by deterioration in the capacitors in the aft HF . Internal arcing between the capacitor plates developed, which vaporised the dielectric medium causing the internal pressure to increase, until it caused the capacitor casing to rupture. Dielectric fluid vapour spr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:e2f26fdf353357a2",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:e9a9185f76f9",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:4b3a114ff733",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:e2f26fdf353357a2",`case_id`:"sd2013_02_control_air",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:8b57dbab2f3af128",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"CASE 2 13MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative During passage, the duty engineer on board a ro-ro passenger ferry noticed an oily mist surrounding one of two air compressors (No1). The compressor in question was supplying control air to the vessel’s main engine clutches. The engineer changed over the supply of control air to a second compres",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:eb171c3e43f0cd6e",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:32aaec3208ad",`target`:"shipkg:vesseltype:1831d47f0525",`properties`:{`name`:"船型为",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:eb171c3e43f0cd6e",`case_id`:"sd2013_12_oily_rag",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:7293e870a8d5467f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"CASE 12 39MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative It was a clear, bright morning as the crew of a small passenger catamaran arrived on board to carry out their routine pre-sailing checks before their first trip of the day. While the master carried out his navigational aids checks, the mate went to the engine rooms and checked the fuel and main engines",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"船型为\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:OF_VESSEL_TYPE {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_46 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:24649f6af55a11fd",`source`:"shipkg:condition:7647f12090ef",`target`:"shipkg:fault:f078b5a27275",`properties`:{`name`:"增加风险",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:24649f6af55a11fd",`case_id`:"sd2016_05_cpp_backup",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:4812bf9684b2b7ad",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"14 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 5 The Lessons 1. Ergonomically, the layout of the bridge console was not well designed. The close proximity of the safety-critical propulsion control buttons and the similar looking everyday use dimmer buttons, increased the likelihood of the type of human error seen in this case. There is always a risk that watchkeepers and equipment operators will inadvertently press the wrong butto",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"增加风险\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": true}"}},{`id`:"edge:740e9eb1e7a243da",`source`:"shipkg:cause:29f8307f5eed",`target`:"shipkg:fault:4e2929b80b35",`properties`:{`name`:"增加风险",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:740e9eb1e7a243da",`case_id`:"finlandia_seaways_me_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:ed4a18d326cb49be",`source_file`:"MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured",`page`:"9",`locator`:"PDF page 9",`quote`:"used to replace the connecting rod small end piston pin bearing bushes by the vessel manager’s maintenance support contractor had introduced stress raisers that signficantly increased the likelihood of crack initiation and fatigue failure. Other factors that contributed to the engine failure included: standards of maintenance management; lack of appreciation of the importance of following the engine manufacturer’s instructions for the removal and refitting of the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"增加风险\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": true}"}},{`id`:"edge:74e694c52d1695ff",`source`:"shipkg:condition:ef4f2a093081",`target`:"shipkg:fault:3349e319bedc",`properties`:{`name`:"增加风险",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:74e694c52d1695ff",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:fc52e39e8b1fe63a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"s. The opportunity to fit the modified flange connection to the external fuel systems on the remaining engines was missed and the risk of fuel leakage remained high. [2.3. 1] 4. Much of the insulation and shielding on all of Stena Europe’s engines was in a poor state of repair or missing completely. The ship’s crew and shore management had become accustomed to this condition over time, possi",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"增加风险\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": true}"}},{`id`:"edge:bc16de904459ec48",`source`:"shipkg:condition:37dbebf86df6",`target`:"shipkg:fault:562580f2bf5a",`properties`:{`name`:"增加风险",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:bc16de904459ec48",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:169a62f5f3bc2de6",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"30",`locator`:"PDF page 30",`quote`:"from the OD box were protected. Critically, in the zone between the two starboard main engines where the leak occurred, there was no evidence after the fire of shielding on the flanged joints. Given the port side arrangement had no shielding for the same joints (Figure 19), it is concluded unlikely that shielding was ever in place on the starboard side. Although surveyed and inspected on a regular basis, the omission",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"增加风险\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": true}"}},{`id`:"edge:d48112dab1dcd5a0",`source`:"shipkg:condition:8012db626950",`target`:"shipkg:fault:256ba55c5fb2",`properties`:{`name`:"增加风险",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:d48112dab1dcd5a0",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:3b167c1e7ff25a89",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"-screw flange within the fuel oil pipework loosened. [2.2] 2. The fuel oil spray was allowed to reach the hot surface because the joint was not protected by anti-splashing tape or shielding and fuel was able to escape forcefully. [2.3.2] 3. The engine manufacturer’s recommended fuel system modification had been fitted to the external fuel system of just one of Stena Europe’s four main engines. The opportunity to fit",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"增加风险\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": true}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:INCREASES_RISK_OF {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_47 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:2567df4a8d750e32",`source`:"shipkg:fault:d005e46c6652",`target`:"shipkg:consequence:7de07882b364",`properties`:{`name`:"加重后果",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:2567df4a8d750e32",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:a61057fac0fe1035",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"51",`locator`:"PDF page 51",`quote`:"e vessel. [2.3.1] 3. The loss of control was exacerbated by the initiation of the pod’s water leakage stop sequence, which led to both pods being parked at 90° to the vessel’s heading. This caused the vessel to lose steerage, its bow to swing to port and its motion to become even more severe. [2.3.1] 4. The vessel’s propulsion control system was unable to prevent the loss of propulsion when its movement was wi",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"加重后果\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": true}"}},{`id`:"edge:7f6a0de1a4eca672",`source`:"shipkg:condition:ff505693e52e",`target`:"shipkg:fault:ae4a492efe41",`properties`:{`name`:"加重后果",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:7f6a0de1a4eca672",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:c2f0061fd7fa1953",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"ation of the CPP system as it maintained the overall system pressure. When this component failed to operate correctly, there were no means within the system to effectively relieve excess pressure. In addition, pressure safety valve (PSV1), which enabled pressure to be dissipated into the return line, was set to operate at 145 bar. This was significantly higher than the pressure at which some parts of the system were able",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"加重后果\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": true}"}},{`id`:"edge:e6b69b6f97a3c827",`source`:"shipkg:condition:f4f364d25a5d",`target`:"shipkg:consequence:196ff2650762",`properties`:{`name`:"加重后果",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:e6b69b6f97a3c827",`case_id`:"sd2016_14_sea_valve",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:fb6cf34a58c7fe85",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"f water ingress to the cargo hold, all six crew abandoned to one of the lifeboats. The vessel continued to flood (Figure 1), with water entering the accommodation areas through the open engine room doorway. The vessel’s owner contracted salvors, who were able to stop the flooding and, once stable, the vessel was towed into port.",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"加重后果\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": true}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:WORSENS {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_48 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:27a54c90ae91058e",`source`:"shipkg:check:b9b23cb93dc6",`target`:"shipkg:condition:4277de3a84c9",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:27a54c90ae91058e",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"reported_action",`certainty_zh`:"报告行动/建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:0917ec321d12afd2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"32",`locator`:"PDF page 32",`quote`:"ght the hazards of entering a fire-damaged space without the correct personal protective equipment. 2024/174 Introduce the use of thermal imaging cameras to all Stena vessels with appropriate functionality for the detection of exposed hot surfaces of over 220°C within machinery spaces. Safety recommendations shall in no case create a presumption of blame or liability.",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:2af65627db2764ce",`source`:"shipkg:check:7bc4821b359e",`target`:"shipkg:fault:72c71c94ca13",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:2af65627db2764ce",`case_id`:"sd2016_22_cooling_pipe",`certainty`:"reported_action",`certainty_zh`:"报告行动/建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:f402f62ae7b113ec",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"60",`locator`:"PDF page 60",`quote`:"a water cooling pipe. Analysis of maintenance records showed that this pipework had not been inspected or renewed for many years. Sea inlet pipework should be thoroughly checked during planned maintenance periods. skipper, who had remained in the wheelhouse, then broadcast a “Mayday” message on VHF radio, which was received and relayed by the coastguard to all vessels in the area. As the vessel began to",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:58661885c40c9a23",`source`:"shipkg:check:b6e1865763c1",`target`:"shipkg:fault:1e5a23a200ad",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:58661885c40c9a23",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported_action",`certainty_zh`:"报告行动/建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:ccd29d6aeef2b43d",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"35",`locator`:"PDF page 35",`quote`:"d PSV3 on all CPP hydraulic modules. • Implemented a maintenance programme in which at least PSV1, PSV3 and NRV6 are disabled and their function checked once every 5 years. • Added a full flow check-valve, with an opening pressure of 10-12 bar, in the return oil circuit by-passing PSV3, the Oil Cooler and NRV6. Also, an additional alarm signal was to be fitted in the control system to give an alarm",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:75841e23b89f0d54",`source`:"shipkg:check:f9cad3df2b98",`target`:"shipkg:cause:8a2abf94d478",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:75841e23b89f0d54",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me2_2018",`certainty`:"derived_action",`certainty_zh`:"依据报告整理的检查建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:d8028bdc4d93a0c8",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"Opportunities to identify and diagnose engine problems early, and therefore avoid catastrophic failures, were missed because the condition of the engine lubricating oil and coolant was not closely monitored. [2.6.2] [2.6.3] 9. Some aspects of the maintenance work carried out by RKM did not meet the standards set by Volvo Penta and those expected by Wightlink. Assembly errors had been made during overhauls, basic levels of workshop c",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:79cc156b4e7adb2e",`source`:"shipkg:check:1c503f83ef89",`target`:"shipkg:condition:6fa538170906",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:79cc156b4e7adb2e",`case_id`:"kommandor_susan_dg1_2025",`certainty`:"derived_action",`certainty_zh`:"依据报告整理的检查建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:1a0b3fbe432ab46d",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"8",`locator`:"PDF page 8",`quote`:"ting priorities during the vessel’s conversion project, this resulted in Hays Ships providing minimal oversight to Holderness and no verification of authenticity for the parts used, enabling the installation of non- OEM components that later contributed to the engine failure. Similar to the lack of oversight highlighted in both the Finlandia Seaways and Finnmaster cases, the lack of structured supervision a",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:7c7bdf8eb11276f2",`source`:"shipkg:check:c55d526e8c4c",`target`:"shipkg:condition:2d0261049d78",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:7c7bdf8eb11276f2",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported_action",`certainty_zh`:"报告行动/建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:8d208881ac72d263",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"69",`locator`:"PDF page 69",`quote`:"possibly leading to a blackout and loss of control in restricted waters, the need for power quality surveillance is significant. Regular monitoring of power quality, using a pre-determined pattern of propulsion motor loading with associated motor operating parameters, would help ensure that the health of electrical equipment on board is closely monitored as the vessel and its equipment ages",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:96a34d6a177bd786",`source`:"shipkg:check:f420d80dbf17",`target`:"shipkg:condition:ed8375f7583f",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:96a34d6a177bd786",`case_id`:"sd2013_02_control_air",`certainty`:"derived_action",`certainty_zh`:"依据报告整理的检查建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:3f0c5814259eb000",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"15",`locator`:"PDF page 15",`quote`:"st 2/2013 The Lessons 1. When starting machinery or when putting machinery on line or on load, it is good engineering practice to check that it is operating correctly. Assumptions often lead to unwanted surprises. 2. When a machinery breakdown occurs in close proximity to navigational dangers and other vessels, its consequences could be catastrophic unless effective action is taken quickly. Ho",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:97769269bb8e8dcd",`source`:"shipkg:check:050d6770cfa0",`target`:"shipkg:condition:52a5771f68ca",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:97769269bb8e8dcd",`case_id`:"sd2016_08_generator_oil",`certainty`:"reported_action",`certainty_zh`:"报告行动/建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:1e3e12480476352c",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"28",`locator`:"PDF page 28",`quote`:"icient to ignite an oil or fuel spray. 2. These temperatures are not visible to the eye unless the surface is glowing. However, a thermal image will immediately identify unlagged sections (Figure 3). 3. All vessels are required to comply with SOLAS regulations regarding the maximum allowable temperature of an exposed surface (Chapter II/2): • All surfaces with temperatures above 220°C which may be impinged as a re",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:9d6285f72a296672",`source`:"shipkg:check:470049664913",`target`:"shipkg:fault:fce2f501a499",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:9d6285f72a296672",`case_id`:"sd2016_09_cpp_response",`certainty`:"reported_action",`certainty_zh`:"报告行动/建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:ec533ae27276b674",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"rried out. These drills will give operators confidence in the back-up systems and help them react effectively in an emergency. 3. Frequent engine response tests should be completed, both ahead and astern. This is particularly important before entering and leaving port or congested waters",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:aa4c596339c6cfa1",`source`:"shipkg:check:5a2af85dcbf4",`target`:"shipkg:fault:b2aa91be158b",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:aa4c596339c6cfa1",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported_action",`certainty_zh`:"报告行动/建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:38d40fe90e8b2dbf",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"69",`locator`:"PDF page 69",`quote`:"when there are no alternative or back-up systems, must fail safe. They should also be tested at regular intervals to verify that all the sub-components in the system are functional. [2.4.5] 7 . Awareness of arc-flash hazards needs to be significantly increased throughout the marine industry, so that designers, builders, owners, operators and engineers understand the hazard, risks and the potential risk redu",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:bf07e6903aa4cc76",`source`:"shipkg:check:fa162d9e9a3f",`target`:"shipkg:cause:0b368a5a5869",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:bf07e6903aa4cc76",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me4_2018",`certainty`:"derived_action",`certainty_zh`:"依据报告整理的检查建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:c74257f47f29e86a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"72",`locator`:"PDF page 72",`quote`:"ble to determine why the technician made such a basic error. However, the engine manufacturer’s investigation identified that the serial numbers on the connecting rods and caps were not routinely checked to ensure that they matched following assembly. To mitigate the risk of similar errors, Volvo Penta introduced an improved method of identifying and matching the connecting rods into its production process. 2.4 OTHER WIGHT CLASS",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:cc0ca93956c2f810",`source`:"shipkg:check:02ead897029b",`target`:"shipkg:fault:58d32c38d0ac",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:cc0ca93956c2f810",`case_id`:"sd2013_05_missing_filter",`certainty`:"derived_action",`certainty_zh`:"依据报告整理的检查建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:b10e854dd960072c",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"ate without any problems and the vessel undertook several voyages. However, after the engine failure, the duplex filter was found without a filter cartridge in the on-line filter chamber, and the engine lubricating oil system was contaminated. The contamination caused main bearing seizure, the rotation of bearing shells and the blockage of oil ways, and subsequent oil starvation and",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:cd1430bee1da21a7",`source`:"shipkg:check:64ccf3c3f401",`target`:"shipkg:fault:dddb0abee018",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:cd1430bee1da21a7",`case_id`:"sd2016_05_cpp_backup",`certainty`:"reported_action",`certainty_zh`:"报告行动/建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:aee93ed7c1866eb1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"id not fully understand the vessel’s propulsion control system and had not routinely tested their back-up and emergency controls. Regular testing of back-up and emergency control systems, and the conduct of machinery breakdown drills, provide the most effective method of ensuring the crew fully understand their ship’s systems and are best prepared to respond in an emergency. Figure 3: Damage to linkspan, mooring",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:d51f41c5677b1145",`source`:"shipkg:check:de8a5b9844ad",`target`:"shipkg:fault:8027eb707475",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:d51f41c5677b1145",`case_id`:"sd2013_03_turning_gear",`certainty`:"derived_action",`certainty_zh`:"依据报告整理的检查建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:d2bfff6df47b53cc",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"18",`locator`:"PDF page 18",`quote`:"2013 The Lessons 1. The turning gear interlock had not been included within the planned maintenance system on board and there was no record of it having been tested. 2. Control console illumination panels are vital to the safe operation of machinery and should therefore be tested regularly. If problems with visual indication or warning lamps cannot be rectified immediately, they must be repo",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:d635d865ca38c4ac",`source`:"shipkg:check:b9cd13a70a15",`target`:"shipkg:fault:c1ffab11185c",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:d635d865ca38c4ac",`case_id`:"sd2016_14_sea_valve",`certainty`:"derived_action",`certainty_zh`:"依据报告整理的检查建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:e7382090fee9962a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"41",`locator`:"PDF page 41",`quote`:"t the valve was fully closed when it was not. Although there was a visual indicator located on the side of the actuator, this was not checked to confirm that the valve was closed prior to removal of the flange bolts. The actuator had previously been repaired. However, the chief engineer, who had only recently joined the vessel, was unaware of the actuator’s poor internal condition (Figures 2 and 3). Figur",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:e60c667ebf1841c7",`source`:"shipkg:check:2ae63dd081a2",`target`:"shipkg:condition:d96dbed6a05c",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:e60c667ebf1841c7",`case_id`:"sd2013_12_oily_rag",`certainty`:"reported_action",`certainty_zh`:"报告行动/建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:f5fbae0eb047725b",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"42",`locator`:"PDF page 42",`quote`:"f waste. Discarded oily materials significantly increase fire risks, especially in hot areas such as engine rooms. 2. Do consider visiting the engine room(s) soon after starting equipment for the first time in the day. Equipment cools down overnight, and restarting it is a vulnerable time because leaks can occur when equipment reaches normal operating temperatures. Also, as this case shows, it provides the opportu",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:eec6461f4fd0dde2",`source`:"shipkg:check:52bfc5553a79",`target`:"shipkg:cause:3667d8d2e0ca",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:eec6461f4fd0dde2",`case_id`:"sd2016_09_cpp_response",`certainty`:"derived_action",`certainty_zh`:"依据报告整理的检查建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:88dffcc589cf9235",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"y to bring the vessel back under control before it struck the quay. It was also revealed during the investigation that the system parameters for astern pitch control had been incorrectly set during the commissioning of the propulsion system when the vessel was delivered from the yard. The Lessons 1. If you are expected to manoeuvre a vessel, you should make every effort to familiarise yourself with the controls at yo",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:f3894185e054e017",`source`:"shipkg:check:3b1fdbe04792",`target`:"shipkg:fault:f2f9d4b10a0b",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:f3894185e054e017",`case_id`:"sd2016_08_generator_oil",`certainty`:"reported_action",`certainty_zh`:"报告行动/建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:7732c1387876e1fb",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"28",`locator`:"PDF page 28",`quote`:"s on the engines exceed acceptable limits. Overall vibration velocity can be measured with very simple instruments. If excessive, frequency analysis of the vibration waveform can often identify the root cause of excessive vibration levels. Figure 3: Example of a thermal image showing ‘hot spots’ on uninsulated sections of the exhaust system",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:f88ba84487c8e409",`source`:"shipkg:check:313a552b87bf",`target`:"shipkg:cause:29f8307f5eed",`properties`:{`name`:"检查",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:f88ba84487c8e409",`case_id`:"finlandia_seaways_me_2018",`certainty`:"derived_action",`certainty_zh`:"依据报告整理的检查建议",`evidence_id`:"ev:33782f93bde6d8a1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured",`page`:"56",`locator`:"PDF page 56",`quote`:"d a competent fitter to undertake the specific task of removing the piston pin bushes at its workshops in Klaipeda. Despite this, seven of the intact 11 small ends removed from Finlandia Seaways’ engine were found to have notch damage on the internal surfaces of their small end eyes. Three of Botnia Seaways’ small ends had similar damage and three had evidence of localised heat damage. Although the technical investigations did not identify when the damage had",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"检查\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:CHECKS {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_49 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:356ae76177cbd32c",`source`:"shipkg:dataset:710ea13e53ac",`target`:"shipkg:source:5137a1994672",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:356ae76177cbd32c",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:1120bc83b6a7d3e0",`source_file`:"Azimuth_Thruster_CBM_Dataset.zip",`source_url`:"https://zenodo.org/records/20101612",`page`:"",`locator`:"README.md",`quote`:"Anonymised vibration, lubricant and availability dataset for tugboat propulsion systems",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:4afc5cad2d503644",`source`:"shipkg:case:213f8edb92c2",`target`:"shipkg:source:b7a22b866ab1",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:4afc5cad2d503644",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:af6ff177f229c6a2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"e suppression spray heads were activated, one in the aft harmonic filter room and the other in the aft main switchboard room. The explosion was triggered by deterioration in the capacitors in the aft HF . Internal arcing between the capacitor plates developed, which vaporised the dielectric medium causing the internal pressure to increase, until it caused the capacitor casing to rupture. Dielectric fluid vapour spr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:647dcdf90cfc8204",`source`:"shipkg:case:1e6479e108d9",`target`:"shipkg:source:159562b24735",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:647dcdf90cfc8204",`case_id`:"kommandor_susan_dg1_2025",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:01f3913bd9c46899",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"f Forth, Scotland on 25 January 2025 SUMMARY At 1305 on 25 January 2025, the site investigation vessel Kommandor Susan suffered a catastrophic failure of a diesel generator engine while conducting sea trials in the Firth of Forth, Scotland. The failure resulted in an engine room fire and a complete power blackout. The crew responded promptly, extinguished the fire and mustered safely. The vessel lost propu",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:64d0a22d1da79381",`source`:"shipkg:case:adf367a46f33",`target`:"shipkg:source:66b61e38c53f",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:64d0a22d1da79381",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me2_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:4846a9af2b7e6456",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"S 3.1 SAFETY ISSUES DIRECTLY CONTRIBUTING TO THE ACCIDENTS THAT HAVE BEEN ADDRESSED OR RESULTED IN RECOMMENDATIONS 1. Wight Sky’s ME2 failed catastrophically due to a sudden loss of lubricating oil supply to its number five main journal bearing and number four crankpin. [2.3.1] 2. The oilway to the main journal and crankpin was blocked off when the bearing shells turned in their housing. Poor fuel combustion, the presence of silic",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:689bc09d8ef4cf1e",`source`:"shipkg:dataset:19e52eb49467",`target`:"shipkg:source:29f30f85af55",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:689bc09d8ef4cf1e",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:ab10a0554fdf6901",`source_file`:"TSRF_main.zip",`source_url`:"https://github.com/TS-RF/TSRF",`page`:"",`locator`:"README.md",`quote`:"Six health states in TSRF data directory; thermodynamic simulation assisted diagnosis",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:74362812a3d7c57b",`source`:"shipkg:case:9676bd22b5e5",`target`:"shipkg:source:a583fceecb4c",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:74362812a3d7c57b",`case_id`:"sd2013_05_missing_filter",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:7116308e5054c090",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"CASE 5 20 MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative A fully loaded cargo ship departed port and proceeded on her voyage. Several days into the passage, the oil mist detector (OMD) on the medium speed diesel main engine alarmed. The duty engineer investigated but could not find any fault with the engine. He",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:7ad4fbbe7b0435da",`source`:"shipkg:case:ad49b658b30b",`target`:"shipkg:source:3f597b4acabc",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:7ad4fbbe7b0435da",`case_id`:"sd2016_14_sea_valve",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:b7715f5c139d9453",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"33 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 14 Fail to Plan, Plan to Fail Narrative On a fine day, a general cargo vessel was on passage with a cargo of limestone. The master was on watch on the bridge. In the engine room, the chief engineer, motorman and a seaman were undertaking maintenance on one of the two main ballast pumps; the chief engineer",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:82e23e98294389fd",`source`:"shipkg:dataset:1ceeb4cad6d8",`target`:"shipkg:source:e12fe2e83b8d",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:82e23e98294389fd",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:b44d9524e09bf0ac",`source_file`:"Marine_Engine_Fault_Data_v1.zip",`source_url`:"https://zenodo.org/records/19857425",`page`:"",`locator`:"dataset_index.csv",`quote`:"MU323DGSC controlled fault scenarios; see dataset_index.csv",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:8444e8fe0865219b",`source`:"shipkg:case:597875e258c6",`target`:"shipkg:source:3f597b4acabc",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:8444e8fe0865219b",`case_id`:"sd2016_05_cpp_backup",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:96829240b9d90823",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"19",`locator`:"PDF page 19",`quote`:"12 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 5 Propelled Onto the Berth Narrative A large roll-on roll-off passenger ferry, operating on its regular route between two European ports, suffered significant damage when it made heavy contact with a linkspan as it was being manoeuvred onto its berth. There were over 500 passengers and crew on board but no",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:8d6898174c890ba2",`source`:"shipkg:case:7a1c0165bb56",`target`:"shipkg:source:3f597b4acabc",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:8d6898174c890ba2",`case_id`:"sd2016_08_generator_oil",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:7e21ab64015c1360",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"26",`locator`:"PDF page 26",`quote`:"19 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 8 Maintenance Induced Fire Narrative A fully loaded ro-ro passenger ferry was en route to its next port when the engineers in the control room acknowledged a low oil pressure alarm on one of the generators (Figure 1). On the CCTV they observed that oil from this generator was spraying on to the adjacen",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:94095f6ec6140b68",`source`:"shipkg:case:537a034e93e3",`target`:"shipkg:source:a583fceecb4c",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:94095f6ec6140b68",`case_id`:"sd2013_03_turning_gear",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:b840391c6c40b9b8",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"CASE 3 15MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative A specialist cargo ship was in port loading a dangerous cargo. As a precaution, the vessel’s slow speed diesel main engine had been tested and was kept at a heightened state of readiness. This involved the fuel being shut off, the main engine indicator",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:9b94cb30ae59d0ec",`source`:"shipkg:case:ffc594a9fab7",`target`:"shipkg:source:a583fceecb4c",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:9b94cb30ae59d0ec",`case_id`:"sd2013_12_oily_rag",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:7293e870a8d5467f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"CASE 12 39MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative It was a clear, bright morning as the crew of a small passenger catamaran arrived on board to carry out their routine pre-sailing checks before their first trip of the day. While the master carried out his navigational aids checks, the mate went to the engine rooms and checked the fuel and main engines",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:9c72d39d5a2669a9",`source`:"shipkg:case:8b13bdb1a5bc",`target`:"shipkg:source:3f597b4acabc",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:9c72d39d5a2669a9",`case_id`:"sd2016_09_cpp_response",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:e1dce2948e24adc9",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"22 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 9 Sluggish Pitch Control Causes Serious Accident Narrative A chemical tanker was being manoeuvred to its designated jetty. As the vessel approached the quay, the pilot ordered an astern movement to enable a turn into the lock. The vessel did not respond and continued to proceed ahead. Despite placing the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:a77cfe20056960be",`source`:"shipkg:case:6f58fb8a8b17",`target`:"shipkg:source:3f597b4acabc",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:a77cfe20056960be",`case_id`:"sd2016_22_cooling_pipe",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:fe1c60aff6da4452",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"59",`locator`:"PDF page 59",`quote`:"52 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 22 Supper Would Have Been on Time if the Vessel Had Not Sunk Narrative A 24m steel hulled fishing trawler, with a crew of six, was fishing in calm seas when its engine began to make unusual noises. No-one was in the wheelhouse; the skipper, who was on watch, had gone to the mess room to prepare supper and the majority of the crew wer",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:aac4e83652fb56a4",`source`:"shipkg:case:551512d967af",`target`:"shipkg:source:a583fceecb4c",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:aac4e83652fb56a4",`case_id`:"sd2013_02_control_air",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:8b57dbab2f3af128",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"CASE 2 13MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative During passage, the duty engineer on board a ro-ro passenger ferry noticed an oily mist surrounding one of two air compressors (No1). The compressor in question was supplying control air to the vessel’s main engine clutches. The engineer changed over the supply of control air to a second compres",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:ac6908ec9f47ee7b",`source`:"shipkg:case:00057f56fe39",`target`:"shipkg:source:21d1480ba4a6",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:ac6908ec9f47ee7b",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me_2017",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:19d0b2283f62b511",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"examination conducted by the vessel’s engine maker, Volvo Penta UK, concluded that the most probable trigger for the failure was debris in the engine’s oil channels following rebuild. The MAIB investigation established the following: • The engine had been completely rebuilt and failed after 5½ hours of operation. • The vessel’s soft patches 1 had not been removed, necessitating the engine to be lowered piecem",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:af433c11952ed610",`source`:"shipkg:case:1f8ffc7c55c3",`target`:"shipkg:source:c33d7f8e3fb6",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:af433c11952ed610",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:8c30394060f9cd2e",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"30",`locator`:"PDF page 30",`quote`:"d, most likely, occurred gradually over a long period of time. 2.3.3 Pipework joints and shielding Whereas the main components of Pride of Canterbury’s CPP system were supplied after testing by the manufacturer, the interconnecting pipework was supplied and fitted by the shipyard when the vessel was constructed. Although the manufacturer’s drawings specified a particular type",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:cd4443bced5710fe",`source`:"shipkg:case:187dc871fbd5",`target`:"shipkg:source:d52922af3fc9",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:cd4443bced5710fe",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:c3429f0fc22579e1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"42",`locator`:"PDF page 42",`quote`:"e vessel’s heading. Given the weather conditions at the time, it is almost certain that Spirit of Discovery’s pitching caused the propellers to come out of the water. This caused a sudden reduction in torque on the propulsion motor and led to a very rapid increase in the motors’ rpm. The engine alarm and monitoring system recorded that, immediately before their shutdown, the rpm of each pod’s",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:d719d5360fcfd4ea",`source`:"shipkg:case:63aa8b018e0d",`target`:"shipkg:source:3d83d6ceacd0",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:d719d5360fcfd4ea",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:57049bc52d7488e2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"7",`locator`:"PDF page 7",`quote`:"mage to the port main engine room and rendered one of its four main engines inoperative for several weeks. The fire was caused by fuel leaking under pressure from the fuel system of main engine number 3 and igniting on an exposed hot surface. No one was injured and there was no pollution. The investigation found that the fuel had ignited on part of the engine’s exhaust system that had",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:d74ebf20cc5e3892",`source`:"shipkg:case:9792cd36162e",`target`:"shipkg:source:af4bce0c23cd",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:d74ebf20cc5e3892",`case_id`:"windcat8_port_engine_2017",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:4e45851ecc9eb9f4",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_01_Windcat8_bearing_failure_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/683922/MAIBInvReport01_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"and no injuries. The MAIB investigation identified that the catastrophic damage to Windcat 8’s port main engine was caused by the failure of a piston connecting rod big end shell bearing, which resulted in the connecting rod assembly releasing and penetrating through the engine crankcase. The investigation also identified that: • A high oil temperature alarm prior to the engine failure warranted a more cautious a",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:d8c026f85cad1492",`source`:"shipkg:dataset:6ab0788d235b",`target`:"shipkg:source:23fd7f407fe4",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:d8c026f85cad1492",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:74d8057daa5c6f01",`source_file`:"UCI_Naval_Propulsion_CBM.zip",`source_url`:"https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/316/condition%2Bbased%2Bmaintenance%2Bof%2Bnaval%2Bpropulsion%2Bplants",`page`:"",`locator`:"README.txt",`quote`:"Frigate gas-turbine propulsion numerical simulator; compressor and turbine decay coefficients",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:e372613b572c153f",`source`:"shipkg:case:278d7572ef08",`target`:"shipkg:source:66b61e38c53f",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:e372613b572c153f",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me4_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:3ca79df2a0332a1a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"igh levels of vibration, and contaminated lubricating oil might all have contributed to the event failure. [2.3.1] 3. Wight Sky’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Volvo Penta’s factory in Sweden. Two of the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:f7d3c136149f9f3e",`source`:"shipkg:case:d6e9f8f8ade2",`target`:"shipkg:source:a4b58f363149",`properties`:{`name`:"记载于",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:f7d3c136149f9f3e",`case_id`:"finlandia_seaways_me_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:eb8d9ba0db21fede",`source_file`:"MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured",`page`:"9",`locator`:"PDF page 9",`quote`:"ent and Incident Investigation Division and the engine manufacturer, MAN Diesel and Turbo SE. The investigation identified that a fracture of the connecting rod small end had led to the sudden failure of the main engine. The investigation also found that the method used to replace the connecting rod small end piston pin bearing bushes by the vessel manager’s maintenance support contractor had intr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"记载于\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:DOCUMENTED_BY {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_50 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:78eb1892f1bf4469",`source`:"shipkg:condition:a9a45fb680fd",`target`:"shipkg:fault:fee4df6aeb24",`properties`:{`name`:"加剧严重度",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:78eb1892f1bf4469",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me2_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:cf454850540d2ce6",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"85",`locator`:"PDF page 85",`quote`:"driving one VSP unit in parallel, because of the time it took the fluid couplings to declutch the shutdown engine. [2.8] 16. The inability to immediately declutch and therefore stop an engine when a shutdown signal was given significantly increased the severity of engine damage and the likelihood of explosions and fires. [2.8] 17. The long history of cavitation erosion and cylinder liner and engine block seal failures",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"加剧严重度\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": true}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:INCREASES_SEVERITY_OF {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_51 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:7a90b3df99d23ffe",`source`:"shipkg:symptom:fa4424a6b543",`target`:"shipkg:fault:f078b5a27275",`properties`:{`name`:"指示",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:7a90b3df99d23ffe",`case_id`:"sd2016_05_cpp_backup",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:b0c29f0e315a7acd",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"19",`locator`:"PDF page 19",`quote`:"continued towards the port. However, a few minutes later the engineers in the engine control room noticed that the starboard CPP back-up control system indicator lamp was illuminated on their console. Having not seen this before, they discussed its significance before deciding to take no immediate action. As the vessel entered the port the master reduced speed by decreasing the pitch settings on the port and",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"指示\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:7b9d6bca057b15ae",`source`:"shipkg:symptom:601948a19d34",`target`:"shipkg:cause:29f8307f5eed",`properties`:{`name`:"指示",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:7b9d6bca057b15ae",`case_id`:"finlandia_seaways_me_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:b2ab413559094e03",`source_file`:"MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured",`page`:"56",`locator`:"PDF page 56",`quote`:"workshops in Klaipeda. Despite this, seven of the intact 11 small ends removed from Finlandia Seaways’ engine were found to have notch damage on the internal surfaces of their small end eyes. Three of Botnia Seaways’ small ends had similar damage and three had evidence of localised heat damage. Although the technical investigations did not identify when the damage had been done, it was clearly apparent that it had be",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"指示\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:95b6f65a0db377d4",`source`:"shipkg:symptom:9d91c2845b73",`target`:"shipkg:fault:d26785dacafa",`properties`:{`name`:"指示",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:95b6f65a0db377d4",`case_id`:"sd2016_08_generator_oil",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:5a52dfb1b2f1d73b",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"26",`locator`:"PDF page 26",`quote`:"arrative A fully loaded ro-ro passenger ferry was en route to its next port when the engineers in the control room acknowledged a low oil pressure alarm on one of the generators (Figure 1). On the CCTV they observed that oil from this generator was spraying on to the adjacent generator. While they were investigating the source of the leak oil that had been sprayed on the exhaust casing of the adjacent en",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"指示\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:bc5f87458313894f",`source`:"shipkg:symptom:89c72d5dc590",`target`:"shipkg:consequence:81fff36694d8",`properties`:{`name`:"指示",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:bc5f87458313894f",`case_id`:"sd2016_22_cooling_pipe",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:e7c09d475a3dc5ea",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"59",`locator`:"PDF page 59",`quote`:"on deck sorting a previous catch. The skipper returned to the wheelhouse to investigate the noises and found that the engine room bilge high level alarm was illuminated and sounding. The skipper instructed the engineer to go to the engine room and investigate. The engineer observed that water was almost level with the top of the main engine and was rising quickly. He started the bilge pump but could not reac",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"指示\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:d1cc2d824057cc25",`source`:"shipkg:symptom:ff3b8fa9a284",`target`:"shipkg:fault:58d32c38d0ac",`properties`:{`name`:"指示",`graph_version`:"2.0",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:d1cc2d824057cc25",`case_id`:"sd2013_05_missing_filter",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:0c984e504147698d",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"23",`locator`:"PDF page 23",`quote`:"e not overlooked. 2. One of the advantages of completing daily logs is the ability to assess trends in the operating machinery. A consistently low reading on the filter differential oil pressure gauge, and a comparison with previous operating hours between filter changes, should have rung alarm bells that something was wrong. 3. An oil mist detector gives advance warning of an impending major failure. When a detector alarm occ",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"指示\", \"graph_version\": \"2.0\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:INDICATES {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_52 }
